1761	\begin{proof}
1762	  The residue pairing (\Cref{thm:adelic_residuePairing}) identifies
1763	  \(\Omega_K(K_C - D)\) with the annihilator of
1764	  \(\mathbb{A}_K(D) + K\), i.e.\ with
1765	  \((\mathbb{A}_K/(\mathbb{A}_K(D) + K))^\ast = \check{H}^1(D)^\ast\)
1766	  (Papaioannou Lemma 1.22; Vater Thm.~1.48), so
1767	  \(\dim_k \Omega_K(K_C - D) = i(D)\). For the first isomorphism, since
1768	  \(\dim_K \Omega_K = 1\) (Papaioannou Thm.~1.23; Vater Thm.~1.48) every
1769	  differential is \(x\omega\) for a unique \(x \in K\); and
1770	  \(\operatorname{div}(x\omega) = \operatorname{div} x + K_C\) (Papaioannou
1771	  Thm.~1.25; Vater Lemma 1.53), so \(x\omega\) lies in
1772	  \(\Omega_K(K_C - D)\) iff \(\operatorname{div} x + K_C \ge K_C - D\) iff
1773	  \(\operatorname{div} x + D \ge 0\) iff \(x \in L(D)\); replacing \(D\) by
1774	  \(K_C - D\) gives that \(\mu\) restricts to a bijection
1775	  \(L(K_C - D) \to \Omega_K(K_C - D)\) (Papaioannou Thm.~1.26; cff
1776	  Thm.~13.5). Composing, \(i(D) = \ell(K_C - D)\).
1777	  \paragraph{Gate.} The construction of \(\Omega_K\), the
1778	  one-dimensionality \(\dim_K \Omega_K = 1\), and the non-degeneracy of
1779	  the pairing are threaded as the single-field class
1780	  \(\mathrm{HasSerreDuality}\, C\) bundling the equivalence \(\mu\);
1781	  Tier 3 consumers verify against it and it is closed by
1782	  \(\texttt{inferInstance}\) once \(\mathrm{HasResiduePairing}\) is discharged.
1783	\end{proof}
